# integration/backlog — nine workstreams, one measured tree (A/B)

Branch `integration/backlog`, based on `merge/read-path` (`3e3665a`) and carrying
the nine backlog workstreams as cherry-picks of each branch's own commits.
Measured build: `fpq-integration` = `sha256:502bcffdd843f193f436b294c9b97486aa546a9c205ee46d7b239fdc79c3274a`
built with:

    flock /tmp/fpq-bench.lock -c \
      'docker build -q --target dev -t fpq-integration -f docker/Dockerfile .'

from the code tree at `37746db` (the records commit that follows this log only
adds this file and `INTEGRATION.md`). Baseline: the existing `fpq-baseline` image,
`sha256:9ae83f61161f`, the protocol baseline the other records use.

Everything below ran on one host, one container at a time, under the same
`flock /tmp/fpq-bench.lock`. Each size is a cold process; `benchmarks.sh` warms
once and reports the median of 3 reps per player. The client's `stream()` is
zero-copy views with nothing consumed; the `PATHS` table reads the same rows
through each of fast-postgres's own interfaces (and ADBC/Arrow's, for scale).

## Commands

    flock /tmp/fpq-bench.lock -c 'docker run --rm --shm-size=3g \
      -e BENCH_GIT_REV=baseline fpq-baseline benchmarks.sh 100000'
    flock /tmp/fpq-bench.lock -c 'docker run --rm --shm-size=3g \
      -e BENCH_GIT_REV=integration fpq-integration benchmarks.sh 100000'
    flock /tmp/fpq-bench.lock -c 'docker run --rm --shm-size=3g \
      -e BENCH_GIT_REV=baseline fpq-baseline benchmarks.sh 1000000'
    flock /tmp/fpq-bench.lock -c 'docker run --rm --shm-size=3g \
      -e BENCH_GIT_REV=integration fpq-integration benchmarks.sh 1000000'

